  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 216 AM EDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\n- Slight chance of Rain Today\n\nA cold front moves through today along with some mid-level \nfrontogenesis. Moisture is limited however and POP have trended\nlower since yesterday. Best chance for rain will be across the\ncentral forecast area this afternoon. Cooler and drier air moves\nin behind the front. With the surface high building in tonight,\nradiational cooling conditions will be optimized and temperatures\nwill fall into the 40s in most places, with even upper 30s possible\nacross the northern interior.\n\n- Showers and Thunderstorms Possible Tuesday through Thursday\n\nA shortwave trough ejects out of the northern Rockies with a\nsurface low tracking into Canada by Tuesday. A trailing cold \nfront is expected to touch off showers and thunderstorms Monday \nnight and Tuesday. Instability and deeper moisture is across \nnorthern Lower Michigan pooling ahead of the cold front, which \nsinks south through the forecast area on Tuesday. Precipitable \nwater surges close 2 inches, so heavy rain potential is there as \nthe front will be moving slowly and MBE vectors are less than 5 \nknots.\n\nThe front stalls across the southern zones on Wednesday, with a\nshowers and thunderstorms possible into Thursday as a surface low\ntracks along the front across southern Lower Michigan.",
